#: app/concept-pages.php:268
msgid "Shops and agencies who want a WordPress site they can edit — not a page-builder mockup. The layout is a starting point; I map it onto your pages, fields, and hosting."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:269
msgid "Built as a Sage 11 WordPress theme: Blade templates, Tailwind v4, Vite for CSS and JS. Visitor copy lives in wp-admin fields, not hardcoded templates. No page builder, no extra options screen."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:270
msgid "You own the theme, the fields, and the repo. I document what to edit in wp-admin so another developer can extend it without reverse-engineering CSS."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:273
msgid "Brokerages, land offices, and independent agents who need listings that are not a generic home-search plugin. The same pattern fits farms, acreage, and historic inventory in Gettysburg — and listings anywhere you already run them."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:274
msgid "Listings are a queryable collection: grid plus map, with filters as URL query args (acreage, township, lot type). Financing widgets are vanilla JavaScript, so they run without a page builder or shortcode pack. The WordPress handoff is a Sage 11 theme. Listings can be a custom post type or an imported feed — the UI does not care as long as the fields exist."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:275
msgid "You own the theme, the listing fields, and the repo. Listing copy, photos, and filters edit in wp-admin. I document the listing schema so another developer can add a filter without touching the template. Rank Math or Yoast owns titles and schema."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:277
msgid "Licensed guides, tour operators, and visitor-facing shops that sell dated tickets instead of a static “call us” page. Built for Gettysburg walking, bus, and lantern tours; the booking pattern ports to other destinations."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:278
msgid "Tours are structured content (not a pile of pages): catalog, filters, and a booking path that can later sit on WooCommerce or a booking plugin. Maps, when present, are a real map library rather than a screenshot. Sage 11 is the WordPress handoff so the same Blade templates keep working after launch."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:279
msgid "You get tour fields, the catalog, and the booking labels in wp-admin. Adding a tour should not require a developer. I leave notes for anything that is not obvious, plus the repo if you want another developer on the theme."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:281
msgid "Independent shops that need a catalog, cart, and checkout they can actually run — not a brochure with a Shop button that goes nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:282
msgid "Catalog, filters, and cart are designed as WooCommerce surfaces. Category and product copy stay in WordPress. The theme is Sage 11 so product templates stay in Git, not in a page builder. Wishlist or filter JS stays small and explicit."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:283
msgid "Products, prices, and photos edit in WooCommerce. I document the product fields and any custom taxonomies. You own the theme zip and can point another developer at the repo."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:285
msgid "Restaurants, taverns, and cafes that need a menu people can scan on a phone, plus a clear path to order or book a table."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:286
msgid "The menu is structured content (sections, items, dietary flags) so it can filter without a PDF. Ordering or reservations hook to a form or a specialist plugin — not a third-party iframe that owns your SEO. Sage 11 keeps the templates in version control."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:287
msgid "Menu items, hours, and photos edit in wp-admin. I document the menu fields so a manager can add a special without calling me. You own the theme and the content."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:289
msgid "Inns, B&Bs, and small hotels that want direct bookings instead of sending every stay to a third-party listing site."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:290
msgid "Rooms are structured content: photos, amenities, and a booking path that can sit on a booking plugin or a simple request form. The marketing pages stay in WordPress so SEO is yours. Sage 11 is the theme layer."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:291
msgid "Room copy, photos, and rates edit in wp-admin. I document the room fields and the booking handoff. You own the theme; another developer can extend availability without rebuilding the front end."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:295
msgid "Land offices, farm brokerages, and agents selling acreage or historic homes who cannot use a suburban MLS skin. Acreline is the WordPress starting point: listings, map, and financing tools aimed at that inventory."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:296
msgid "Listings render as a grid and a map, with acreage, township, and lot-type filters as query args. The land-loan estimate and pre-qualification widgets are vanilla JS. Intended production stack is Sage 11, a listing CPT or imported feed, and Rank Math for titles and schema. No page builder, no IDX chrome unless we wire a real feed later."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:297
msgid "You own the theme and the listing fields. Brokers edit parcels, photos, and copy in wp-admin. I document the listing schema (filters, map pin fields, financing copy) so the next developer can extend it. Hire me to map this onto your inventory, or start from the public demo and tell me what to change."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:302
#, php-format
msgid "Can I start from %s?"
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:303
msgid "Yes. Say which project and what you would change. I map the layout onto your WordPress site — pages you can edit, a theme you own, no page builder."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:306
msgid "What do I edit in WordPress after launch?"
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:307
msgid "Copy, photos, hours, and listings live in wp-admin. I add fields for anything that needs to change on a regular basis, and I write a short note for the rest."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:310
msgid "Do I get the source theme?"
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:311
msgid "Yes. A production build is a Sage theme you own, plus the field map. Public demos stay examples; the paid build is yours to host and extend."
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:314
msgid "Is this a live client site?"
msgstr ""

#: app/concept-pages.php:315
msgid "No. It is an example project on matthummel.com. Hire me to adapt it for your shop, or use it as the brief for an agency overflow job."
msgstr ""

